**Files:** `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/errors.spec.ts` and `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/api-errors.spec.ts`

**Key Patterns for Error Induction:**

#### Pattern 1: Direct `page.route()` for Mocking Specific Endpoints
```typescript
// From errors.spec.ts lines 22-31
await page.route('**/api/tasks/@invalid-task', (route) => {
  route.fulfill({
    status: 404,
    contentType: 'application/json',
    body: JSON.stringify({
      error: 'not_found',
      message: 'Task not found: @invalid-task',
      suggestion: 'Did you mean @task-setup?'
    })
  });
});
```

#### Pattern 2: Conditional Route Interception by HTTP Method
```typescript
// From errors.spec.ts lines 63-80
await page.route('**/api/inbox', (route) => {
  if (route.request().method() === 'POST') {
    route.fulfill({
      status: 400,
      contentType: 'application/json',
      body: JSON.stringify({
        error: 'validation_error',
        details: [
          { field: 'text', message: 'Text is required' },
          { field: 'text', message: 'Text must be at least 3 characters' }
        ]
      })
    });
  } else {
    // Pass through GET requests
    route.continue();
  }
});
```

#### Pattern 3: Direct Fetch in API Tests
```typescript
// From api-errors.spec.ts lines 38-56 (using playwright request fixture)
const response = await request.get(`${DAEMON_URL}/api/tasks/@nonexistent-ref-xyz`);
expect(response.status()).toBe(404);
const body = await response.json();
expect(body).toHaveProperty('error');
expect(body.error).toBe('not_found');
```

**Error Types Tested:**
- **404 Not Found** with `{error, message, suggestion}` structure
- **400 Validation Errors** with `{error, details: [{field, message}]}` array
- **409 State Transition** errors with `{error, current, valid_transitions}`

---

### 3. Loading Skeleton and Deterministic Network Handling

**Loading Skeleton Components:**

1. **Generic Skeleton** (`/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/src/lib/components/ui/skeleton/skeleton.svelte`):
   ```svelte
   <div
     bind:this={ref}
     data-slot="skeleton"
     class={cn("bg-accent animate-pulse rounded-md", className)}
     {...restProps}
   ></div>
   ```
   Uses `animate-pulse` CSS for visual feedback.

2. **Command Loading** (`/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/src/lib/components/ui/command/command-loading.svelte`):
   ```svelte
   <CommandPrimitive.Loading bind:ref {...restProps} />
   ```

**Deterministic Loading Patterns in E2E Tests:**

#### Pattern 1: Wait for Network Idle
```typescript
// From triage.spec.ts lines 40-52
async function reloadWithRetry(page, attempts = 3) {
  for (let attempt = 1; attempt <= attempts; attempt++) {
    try {
      await page.reload();
      await page.waitForLoadState('networkidle');
      return;
    } catch (error) {
      if (attempt === attempts) {
        throw error;
      }
      await page.waitForTimeout(250 * attempt);
    }
  }
}
```

#### Pattern 2: Wait for Specific Element Visibility
```typescript
// From dashboard.spec.ts lines 70-74
await page.goto('/');
await expect(page.getByTestId('task-count-ready')).not.toContainText('...');
```

#### Pattern 3: Debounce Testing with Explicit Timeout Waits
```typescript
// From search.spec.ts lines 64-84
test('debounces search by 300ms', async ({ page }) => {
  // Type search query
  await input.fill('task');

  // Results should NOT appear immediately (within 200ms)
  await page.waitForTimeout(200);

  // Wait for debounce (100ms more = 300ms total)
  await page.waitForTimeout(150);
});
```

#### Pattern 4: Conditional Loading State Display
```typescript
// From specs/+page.svelte lines 80-86
{#if loading}
  <div class="space-y-4">
    <Skeleton class="h-12 w-full" />
    <Skeleton class="h-12 w-full" />
    <Skeleton class="h-12 w-full" />
    <Skeleton class="h-12 w-full" />
  </div>
```

**No explicit network throttling** — E2E tests rely on daemon actual response times or use `waitForLoadState('networkidle')` for determinism.

---

### 4. Empty State Patterns When Collections Are Empty

**Pattern: Conditional Empty State Messages**

#### TaskList Component (`/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/src/lib/components/TaskList.svelte` lines 79-85):
```svelte
{#if tasks.length === 0}
  <TableRow>
    <TableCell colspan={6} class="text-center text-muted-foreground">
      No tasks found
    </TableCell>
  </TableRow>
{:else}
  <!-- render tasks -->
{/if}
```

#### Inbox View (`/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/src/routes/inbox/+page.svelte` lines 208-212):
```svelte
{:else if items.length === 0}
  <div class="text-center text-muted-foreground">
    <p>No inbox items.</p>
    <p class="text-sm">Click "Add Item" to capture ideas and thoughts.</p>
  </div>
```

#### Spec Items Tree (`/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/src/lib/components/ItemTree.svelte` lines 134-142):
```svelte
<div class="space-y-1" data-testid="spec-tree-container">
  {#if items.length === 0}
    <p class="text-center text-muted-foreground py-8">No spec items found</p>
  {:else}
    <div class="space-y-1" data-testid="spec-tree">
      {#each tree as node (node.item._ulid)}
        {@render renderNode(node, 0)}
      {/each}
    </div>
  {/if}
</div>
```

#### Command Palette Empty State (`/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/src/lib/components/CommandPalette.svelte` lines 121-145):
```svelte
<Command.List data-testid="command-palette-results">
  {#if loading}
    <Command.Loading>Searching...</Command.Loading>
  {:else if query.trim() && results.length === 0}
    <Command.Empty>No results found.</Command.Empty>
  {:else}
    <!-- render grouped results -->
  {/if}
</Command.List>
```

**Empty State Features:**
1. **User-friendly messages** with actionable guidance (e.g., "Click 'Add Item' to capture ideas")
2. **Semantic HTML** with `text-muted-foreground` class for visual de-emphasis
3. **Consistent pattern**: `{#if loading}` → `{:else if items.length === 0}` → `{:else}` render data
4. **Test-friendly**: Uses `data-testid` for verification
5. **No hidden elements** — empty states are fully visible when collection is truly empty (feature enabled but empty)

#### Related Error State (`/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/src/routes/specs/+page.svelte` lines 87-95):
```svelte
{:else if error}
  <div
    class="rounded-md border border-destructive bg-destructive/10 p-4"
    data-testid="error-message"
    role="alert"
  >
    <p class="text-destructive font-medium">Error loading spec items</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-destructive/80">{error}</p>
  </div>
```

